Package: dev.airdevs.dsh-app
Name: DeepSeek Harness
Version: 0.2.2-rc.3+ios18
Section: Applications
Priority: optional
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Air-Devs <air2@localhost>
Depends: dev.airdevs.dsh (>= 0.2.1-rc.5+ios14)
Description: The DeepSeek Harness full-screen app for iOS (deb / SpringBoard .app form).
 One Home Screen icon. Tapping it shows the unchanged DSH Web UI in a
 standalone full-screen Web Clip (FullScreen=true, no Safari bars), with
 workspace, sessions and plugins loaded normally from the on-device Harness
 host. A launchd keep-alive daemon plus a fixed loopback launch token let the
 static Web Clip URL authenticate on rc.3 (303 + HttpOnly cookie), so no
 terminal and no per-launch token copying are needed.
 The native SFSafariViewController shell in this package is only a fallback
 opener and daemon bootstrapper; it is NOT the full-screen entry (it always
 shows Safari bars). The 125 MB Node/DSH runtime is the existing
 dev.airdevs.dsh engine dependency, the same role Electron's bundled Node
 plays in the official desktop app.
 Installing, launching and removing this package never writes $DSH_HOME:
 conversations, workspaces, plugins and profiles are left byte-for-byte.
Homepage: https://github.com/yitenchen123/dsh-ios
